# Single source of truth for the llama.cpp toolchain this repo builds against.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#
# `local-llm` links libllama / libllama-common / libggml / libggml-base, and
# CLlamaBridge.cpp compiles against vendored llama.cpp headers. Before this pin,
# those libraries came from `brew install llama.cpp` with no version constraint,
# which means the version was "whatever was current the day you ran it" and was
# not expressible in the repo at all. Two contributors cloning the same commit a
# few weeks apart got different ABIs; the symptom is a compile error such as
# `no member named 'use_mmap' in 'llama_model_params'` on an unmodified tree.
#
# Homebrew cannot fix this, because it cannot install a specific llama.cpp
# version: there is no versioned formula, the core tap is API-only so there is
# no local formula history to check out, `brew pin` only freezes whatever you
# already have, and `ggml` is a separate formula that must move in lockstep.
# Through Homebrew the repo could declare and detect a version, never deliver
# one.
#
# So Homebrew is no longer involved. scripts/provision-llama.sh downloads the
# release asset named below from GitHub, verifies it against the sha256 here,
# and assembles a repo-local prefix at `.llama/current`. GitHub release assets
# are immutable, so every contributor and CI run gets identical bytes, and
# nothing `brew upgrade` does can move the build off this pin.
#
# WHY THE UPSTREAM RELEASE ASSET AND NOT A HOMEBREW BOTTLE
#
# Bottles were tried first and do not work when pulled outside Homebrew.
# Homebrew builds ggml with `-DGGML_BACKEND_DL=ON -DGGML_BACKEND_DIR=<libexec>`,
# so the Metal/CPU/BLAS compute backends are dlopen'd plugins in `libexec/` and
# that directory is a compile-time string baked into the dylib. Relocating the
# bottle cannot rewrite it (install_name_tool only edits Mach-O load commands),
# so zero backends register and every model load fails instantly. The upstream
# release is built with `GGML_BACKEND_DL=OFF`: the backends are ordinary linked
# dylibs under `lib/`, with `@rpath` install names throughout, which also means
# no install_name_tool and no re-signing are needed. It has no external formula
# dependencies (no libomp, no openssl) and is built `minos 13.3`, comfortably
# under this repo's macOS 15.0 deployment floor.
#
# WHY THE HEADERS ARE NOT LISTED HERE
#
# The binary release asset contains dylibs, CLI executables and LICENSE only —
# zero headers. They are vendored in-repo instead, so provisioning stays a
# single immutable download; see local-llm/third_party/llama_cpp_api/COMMIT for
# the full reasoning. LLAMA_CPP_COMMIT below records the commit those vendored
# headers came from, and provision-llama.sh fails closed if it disagrees with
# what the vendored trees declare.
#
# TO BUMP THIS PIN
#
#   1. Pick a release from https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/releases
#      and resolve its commit:
#        gh api repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/git/refs/tags/b<new> --jq '.object.sha'
#   2. Get the asset's sha256:
#        curl -fsSL -o /tmp/llama.tar.gz \
#          https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/releases/download/b<new>/llama-b<new>-bin-macos-arm64.tar.gz
#        shasum -a 256 /tmp/llama.tar.gz
#   3. Update LLAMA_CPP_RELEASE, LLAMA_CPP_COMMIT and LLAMA_CPP_SHA256 below.
#   4. Re-vendor BOTH header sets from that same commit:
#        local-llm/third_party/llama_cpp_api/COMMIT
#        local-llm/Sources/CLlamaBridge/third_party/llama_cpp_common/COMMIT
#   5. rm -rf .llama && ./scripts/provision-llama.sh
#   6. cd local-llm && swift test    # 21 tests, real inference — catches ABI drift
#
# Expect upstream API churn at step 6; that is the point of pinning. b9200 to
# b10330 needed two edits in CLlamaBridge.cpp (`use_mmap` became the
# `llama_load_mode` enum; `llama_sampler_init_penalties` regained a leading
# `n_vocab` parameter).

LLAMA_CPP_RELEASE=b10330
LLAMA_CPP_COMMIT=687e7789271ec1276e3470f158428e11a4f80b6f
LLAMA_CPP_ASSET=llama-b10330-bin-macos-arm64.tar.gz
LLAMA_CPP_SHA256=0b107ef13b2f5a20f5538a98ab9a2606b7bbe90824da0f7818a1059e6229cf64
